{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ומלא חפניו", :translit "u'mele khapnav", :gloss "and he shall fill his palms"} {:he "ומלא החבל", :translit "u'mele hechevel", :gloss "and he shall fill the rope"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Masoretic parallel: same phrase ומלא appears with חפניו here and with החבל in the Joab narrative"}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'and he shall fill the rope' (ומלא החבל) does not occur in any biblical passage linked to Joab. The link between Yom Kippur atonement and military victory is expressed at Leviticus 16:30, 'for on this day he shall atone for you,' which the midrash reads as granting merit that extends beyond the sanctuary.", :sources ["Leviticus 16:30"]}} {:quotes [{:he "סמים דקה", :translit "samim dakah", :gloss "fine spices"} {:he "דקה", :translit "dakah", :gloss "fine"} {:he "מדקה", :translit "medukah", :gloss "from crushing"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "דקה", :b "מדקה"}], :frame {:text "The ketoret is described as 'pure and crushed' at Exodus 30:36 (ודקה מדכה in some traditions), emphasizing that the spices must be finely pulverized. Ba'al HaTurim reads the adjective דקה as containing an allusion, via gematria, to מדקה, the crushed form required for the incense.", :sources ["Exodus 30:36" "Exodus 30:35"]}} {:quotes [{:he "דקה", :translit "dakah", :gloss "fine"} {:he "ואחר האש קול דממה דקה", :translit "v'achar ha'esh kol demamah dakah", :gloss "and after the fire a sound of thin silence"} {:he "כי בענן אראה על הכפורת", :translit "ki b'anan era'eh al hakaporet", :gloss "for in a cloud I will appear upon the cover"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["דקה"]}], :frame {:text "The word דקה appears in the incense portion of the Yom Kippur service (Leviticus 16:12) and in Elijah's revelation at 1 Kings 19:12 ('a sound of thin silence'). The cloud of incense upon the cover (Leviticus 16:13, 'for in a cloud I will appear upon the cover') is linked by Ba'al HaTurim to the divine manifestation Elijah experienced, both described with the word דקה.", :sources ["Leviticus 16:12" "Leviticus 16:13" "1 Kings 19:12"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Masoretic parallel: same phrase ומלא appears with חפניו here and with החבל in the Joab narrative", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "דקה", :a-value 109, :b "מדקה", :b-value 149, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["דקה"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "דקה", :refs ["Leviticus 16:12" "1 Kings 19:12"], :n 2, :lens :exact}]}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:24:04.724089597Z", :model "glm-5.2"}